e pattern `git diff` and `git diff *` are allowed. `git diff` alone should match `git diff` pattern... actually the allow list has `\"pattern\":\"git diff\"` which matches exactly \"git diff\". And `git diff *` matches git diff followed by args. Let me run `git diff` — that should be allowed.\n\nActually, let me be careful about how the pattern matching works. The rule `git diff` might match a command starting with \"git diff\" as a prefix, or exactly. Given `git diff *` is separately listed, `git diff` alone is its own entry. I'll run `git diff` and `git diff --stat`.\n\nLet me get the full diff to understand changes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1379736b7001ltHEdbuvoHw6dp","sessionID":"ses_ec869172affeZ2EyFY2MELrMQp","messageID":"msg_13797266c001Ua45QaGP5mfym0"}}
